 "questions": [
  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "L01_001_Print Hello",
   "display_name": "Print Hello",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Welcome to your very first Python programming question! &#128512;</p>\n<p>In this question, you simply need to <b>print</b> the word <code>Hello</code> on the screen.</p>\n<p>In Python, we use the <code>print()</code> function to display text. For example, if you write:</p>\n<pre>print(\"Good Morning\")</pre>\n<p>it will display:</p>\n<pre>Good Morning</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Write a one-line Python program that displays exactly the word <code>Hello</code> (without the quotes).</p>\n<p><b>Expected Output:</b></p>\n<pre>Hello</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "Hello",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "L01_002_Print Hello World",
   "display_name": "Print Hello World",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Almost every programmer's first program is the famous \"Hello, World!\" program. Let's write yours!</p>\n<p>You need to print the exact text <code>Hello, World!</code> including the comma and the exclamation mark.</p>\n<p>Example: If we asked you to print <code>Good Morning!</code>, your code would be:</p>\n<pre>print(\"Good Morning!\")</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Write a Python program that prints exactly:</p>\n<pre>Hello, World!</pre>\n<p>Be careful with punctuation and spacing - the output must match exactly!</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "Hello, World!",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L01_003_Greet By Name",
   "display_name": "Greet By Name",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's make our program interactive! Instead of always printing the same thing, we will read the user's name and greet them personally.</p>\n<p>Use <code>input()</code> to read a line of text typed by the user, and store it in a variable. For example:</p>\n<pre>city = input()\nprint(\"Welcome to \" + city)</pre>\n<p>If the user types <code>Paris</code>, this prints:</p>\n<pre>Welcome to Paris</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read the user's name (a single line of text) and print a greeting in the exact format <code>Hello, &lt;name&gt;!</code></p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>Alice</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>Hello, Alice!</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>Bob</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>Hello, Bob!</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Alice",
     "expected": "Hello, Alice!",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Bob",
     "expected": "Hello, Bob!",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Zara",
     "expected": "Hello, Zara!",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "L01_004_Echo A Number",
   "display_name": "Echo A Number",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Numbers typed by the user through <code>input()</code> are read as <b>text (strings)</b> by default, even if they look like numbers! To use them as actual numbers, we must convert them using <code>int()</code>.</p>\n<p>For example:</p>\n<pre>x = int(input())\nprint(x)</pre>\n<p>If the user enters <code>7</code>, this program reads the text <code>\"7\"</code>, converts it into the whole number <code>7</code> using <code>int()</code>, and prints <code>7</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read one whole number from the user and print it back out, exactly as given.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>5</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>5</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
