   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 5,
   "xml_name": "L01_005_Double The Number",
   "display_name": "Double The Number",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now that you know how to read a number using <code>int(input())</code>, let's do some simple arithmetic with it!</p>\n<p>In Python, <code>*</code> is used for multiplication. For example, <code>n * 2</code> gives you double the value of <code>n</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number and print double its value.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>4</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>8</pre>\n<p>(because 4 doubled is 8)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
