  {
   "xml_index": 10,
   "xml_name": "L01_010_Integer Division",
   "display_name": "Integer Division",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>When we divide one whole number by another and want a <b>whole number</b> result (ignoring anything after the decimal point), we use the <b>integer division</b> operator <code>//</code> in Python.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>7 // 2</code> gives <code>3</code> (not 3.5), because integer division drops the fractional/remainder part.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole, positive numbers (one per line) and print the result of integer-dividing the first by the second.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>7\n2</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>3</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
