  {
   "xml_index": 11,
   "xml_name": "L01_011_Remainder Modulus",
   "display_name": "Remainder Modulus",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Sometimes we want to know what is <b>left over</b> after dividing one number by another. Python gives us this using the <b>modulus operator</b> <code>%</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>7 % 2</code> gives <code>1</code>, because when 7 is divided by 2, the quotient is 3 and the remainder is 1.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole, positive numbers (one per line) and print the remainder when the first is divided by the second.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>7\n2</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>1</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
