  {
   "xml_index": 12,
   "xml_name": "L01_012_Average Two Numbers",
   "display_name": "Average Two Numbers",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>average</b> of two numbers is found by adding them together and dividing by 2. In Python, the regular division operator <code>/</code> always gives a result with a decimal point (a \"float\"), even if the numbers divide evenly.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>7 / 2</code> gives <code>3.5</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole numbers (one per line) and print their average.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>3\n4</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>3.5</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
