  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L01_013_Area Of Circle",
   "display_name": "Area Of Circle",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use what you have learned to solve a small real-world problem: finding the area of a circle!</p>\n<p>The formula for the area of a circle, given its radius <code>r</code>, is:</p>\n<pre>area = 3.14 * r * r</pre>\n<p>(Here we use 3.14 as an approximate value of pi.)</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read the radius of a circle (a whole number) and print its area using the formula above.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>5</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>78.5</pre>\n<p>(because 3.14 * 5 * 5 = 78.5)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
