  {
   "xml_index": 15,
   "xml_name": "L01_015_Celsius To Fahrenheit",
   "display_name": "Celsius To Fahrenheit",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Weather temperatures can be measured in Celsius or Fahrenheit. The formula to convert a temperature from Celsius (C) to Fahrenheit (F) is:</p>\n<pre>F = C * 9 / 5 + 32</pre>\n<p><strong>Your task:</strong> Read a temperature in Celsius (a whole number) and print the equivalent temperature in Fahrenheit.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>0</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>32.0</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>100</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>212.0</pre>",
