   "xml_name": "L01_018_Simple Interest",
   "display_name": "Simple Interest",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In banking and finance, <b>Simple Interest (SI)</b> is calculated using the formula:</p>\n<pre>SI = (Principal * Rate * Time) / 100</pre>\n<p>where <b>Principal</b> is the amount of money, <b>Rate</b> is the interest rate per year (in percent), and <b>Time</b> is the duration in years.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read the principal, rate, and time (three whole numbers, one per line, in that order) and print the simple interest.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>1000\n5\n2</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>100.0</pre>\n<p>(because (1000 * 5 * 2) / 100 = 100.0)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
