   "display_name": "Age Plus Minus Ten",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's finish Lab 1 with a fun little program about age!</p>\n<p>Given a person's current age, we want to know:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Their age 10 years from now (current age + 10)</li>\n<li>Their age 10 years ago (current age - 10)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read the current age (a whole number). First print the age 10 years from now, then on the next line print the age 10 years ago.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>20</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>30\n10</pre>\n<p>(because 20 + 10 = 30, and 20 - 10 = 10)</p>\n<p>Note: the \"age 10 years ago\" can even be negative if the current age is less than 10 - don't worry, your formula still works correctly in that case!</p>",
